---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
const anatomy = [['01', 'House number', '4712', 'Drawn from a plausible local numbering range instead of an arbitrary long number.'], ['02', 'Street name', 'Juniper Ridge Rd', 'Built from words and road suffixes that fit the selected region.'], ['03', 'City and postal code', 'Raleigh, NC 27613', 'City, region abbreviation and postal format remain coherent.'], ['04', 'Phone number', '+1 (919) 555-0164', 'Country code, area code and grouping follow the chosen country.']];
---
<Layout locale="en" title="Address and test identity generator · NodeMail">
  <section class="identity-hero"><div class="shell identity-hero-grid"><div data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">ADDRESS FORMAT · TEST IDENTITY</p><h1 class="product-display">Every field looks local,<br /><span>none of it is you.</span></h1><p class="product-lede">Generate a coherent set of placeholder names, streets, postal codes and phone numbers for development, demos and forms that do not require legal identity.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href={site.appOrigin}>Generate an identity</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="#anatomy">See how it is built</a></div></div><div class="map-visual" data-reveal aria-label="Address format visualization"><div class="map-grid-lines"></div><span class="map-block b1"></span><span class="map-block b2"></span><span class="map-block b3"></span><span class="map-block b4"></span><span class="map-block b5"></span><span class="map-block b6"></span><span class="map-cross horizontal"></span><span class="map-cross vertical"></span><span class="map-pin"></span><div class="map-address-card"><small>NODEMAIL · 27613</small><code>4712 Juniper Ridge Rd<br />Raleigh, NC 27613<br />+1 (919) 555-0164</code></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section section-soft" id="anatomy"><div class="shell"><div class="section-heading" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">ANATOMY OF AN ADDRESS</p><h2>Assembled from rules, not random noise</h2><p>Each field follows the basic structure of its region, and the complete set stays internally consistent.</p></div><div class="anatomy-list">{anatomy.map(([no, label, value, text]) => <div class="anatomy-row" data-reveal><span>{no}</span><small>{label}</small><strong>{value}</strong><p>{text}</p></div>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell detail-split"><div class="section-heading" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">BOUNDARY</p><h2>Formatted correctly does not mean legally real</h2></div><div class="detail-copy" data-reveal><p>Use generated data only for development, testing, demonstrations and placeholders. Never use it for financial, government, identity verification or any process that legally requires your real details.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="cta-band"><div class="shell cta-inner" data-reveal><h2>Choose a country and generate</h2><p>Eight countries and regions use their own postal, address and phone formats.</p><div class="cta-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/en/address-generator/">Open the address generator</a></div></div></section>
</Layout>
